// Authored physical-channel associations; geometry and movement permissions resolve from saved PATH evidence.
// One physical track keeps its channel ID at its exposed ends; each directed member and edge cut has its own local ID.
// Fan channels continue north-to-west and east-to-north. Merge branches enter their matching mainline only through saved journeys.
// Paired ends use native flat L2 defaults. Single curved cuts deliberately have no perpendicular/paired profile.
// A curved cut carries its measured position and heading; it is not an ordinary straight joining boundary.
// Separate branch channels can merge into a mainline track only through the measured internal journeys.
